      "text": "Because the café sells new household goods at lower prices than local shops.",  
      "why_wrong": "The café does not sell new items—it only repairs old ones; this misrepresents the café’s purpose entirely."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Because the town council has banned all new product sales in Millbrook.",  
      "why_wrong": "The council has not banned new sales; it is only reviewing the café’s permit, and no such ban is mentioned in the text."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Because people are using the café to steal items from local stores.",  
      "why_wrong": "There is no evidence or suggestion of theft; the café is a legitimate community initiative focused on repair, not theft."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Because the café discourages people from shopping by hosting events on weekends.",  
      "why_wrong": "The café’s events are not described as discouraging shopping; in fact, it’s the repair activity, not the timing, that affects sales."  
    },  
    {  
      "text": "Because the café provides free replacements for all broken household goods.",  
      "why_wrong": "The café repairs items, not replaces them; the text clearly distinguishes between repair and replacement, making this a fundamental misunderstanding."  
